{"@context":["https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/ns/content/v1.jsonld",{"@base":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio/"}],"@id":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/prop-q-resolvent-unique","@type":["folio-assistant-core:Proposition","doco:Section"],"label":"prop:q-resolvent-unique","kind":"proposition","title":"Uniqueness of the $q$-resolvent","uses":["papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/prop-q-resolvent-exists"],"proofs":["papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/prf-q-resolvent-unique"],"tags":["uniqueness","resolvent"],"leanRef":"qou:QOU.QResolvent.unique","text":"q-resolvent-unique.md","leanSource":"q-resolvent-unique.lean","provenance":"authored","html":"<p><a id=\"prop:q-resolvent-unique\"></a>\n<strong>Proposition.</strong> <em>Uniqueness of the <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">q</code>-resolvent</em></p>\n<p>The <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">q</code>-resolvent <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">R_q(s)</code> is the unique morphism satisfying <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">(s + \\widehat{\\Delta_q}) \\circ R_q(s) = \\mathrm{id}</code>.</p>\n"}
